From 59edeb2eb5d7a6df20972daa6ea5801b67f391cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:26:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc, rom: IPv6 coverage, dual-stack DNS health, cross-network
 names, the DDNS firewall wipe, private /tmp, no app network installer

- IPv6: Gatekeeper's captive check, Service Intercept, the watchdog, SNMP and
  DHCPv6 names work over IPv6; per-network IPv6 switch respected.
- DNS health check: both faces of a dual-stack LAN resolver are probed every
  tick and moved independently; the intercept gate closes per address family;
  nothing touches the IPv6 side while IPv6 is off.
- Reverse DNS across networks (main LAN <-> each VLAN, never VLAN <-> VLAN,
  never guest/portal) and IPv6 device names (rv6names: neighbour cache +
  DHCPv4 names -> each network's addn-hosts file, one reload on change).
- Stock stop_ddns() re-restored the whole filter table from an old snapshot,
  silently deleting guest isolation, Gatekeeper, Warden and the rules engine on
  every DDNS stop; it now deletes only its own rule.
- The watchdog's rules-engine heal was refused by reaper_lockrun (script not
  allowlisted); now listed. Tunnel-aware first-hop note.
- /tmp hardening (audit F1/F2/V3): fs.protected_* on at boot, every Reaper
  directory created root-only at boot and checked at use, Reaper's loose files
  moved into /tmp/reaper, err_rules 0700, scripts run only when root-owned and
  private (incl. PBR's runner and reaper_lockrun), chain names from chainsig
  validated, the restore's staged settings created fresh, IPv6 names written
  atomically.
- rom: the app network installer is not shipped (audit V11: plain-HTTP packages
  run as root; the vendor HTTPS host serves an incomplete chain) - nine scripts
  dropped, rc refuses install/update/upgrade/switch/cancel; the USB chain, disk
  check and removal of an installed app are kept. The firmware download is
  created under umask 022 and must be a private root file before the flash; the
  update check keeps its manifest and key in /tmp/reaper.
- usb.c: bounded /proc/partitions scans; create_custom_passwd closes its file
  and checks the group file open (stock hygiene, unreachable).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
